    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. so if i'm looking at how the world actually became 'modern' and how these different systems eventually merged into the global standards we see today, would it be accurate to say that most of these non-western advancements were just stepping stones that eventually paved the way for the more systematic scientific and legal revolutions that happened in the west? like, was the west the main driver that consolidated all these different ideas into the modern world?",
